## Why This Is Asked

Tests readiness for PQC adoption, key management at scale, and edge trust boundaries across multiple regions and tenants.

 ## Key Concepts

- Algorithm agility and hybrid signing
- Per-tenant key lifecycle in HSM/KMS
- Remote attestation and secure RNG
- Cross-region key rotation and revocation
- SBOM maintenance and incident response planning

 ## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: hybrid signing for PQC migration
function signPayload(payload, tenantId) {
  const keys = getTenantKeys(tenantId); // { legacyKey, pqcKey, phase }
  if (phase === 'migration') {
    return signWithLegacy(payload, keys.legacyKey) + signWithPQC(payload, keys.pqcKey);
  } else {
    return signWithPQC(payload, keys.pqcKey);
  }
}
```

 ## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure migration latency and plan rollback?
- What tests validate cross-region key revocation effectiveness?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical security fundamentals at junior level with real-world constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Rate limiting and lockout; constant-time comparisons; password hashing; MFA basics; secure logging/privacy.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo login flow illustrating bcrypt compare, MFA, and session issuance
async function login(req, res) {
  const { username, password, mfaToken } = req.body;
  const user = await getUser(username);
  if (!user) return res.status(401).send('Invalid credentials');
  const ok = await bcrypt.compare(password, user.hash);
  if (!ok) return res.status(401).send('Invalid credentials');
  if (user.mfaEnabled) {
    if (!mfaToken) return res.status(401).send('MFA required');
    const verified = speakeasy.totp.verify({ secret: user.mfaSecret, encoding: 'base32', token: mfaToken });
    if (!verified) return res.status(401).send('Invalid MFA');
  }
  const session = createSession(user.id);
  res.cookie('session', session, { httpOnly: true, secure: true });
  return res.send({ ok: true });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for distributed rate limiting?
- How would you test lockout and recovery flows?
- How would you store and rotate MFA seeds securely?

## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses understanding of insider threat mitigation and cryptographic key management at scale in multi-tenant environments.

## Key Concepts
- Envelope encryption for efficient large-scale data protection
- Per-tenant Data Encryption Keys (DEKs) for tenant isolation
- Regional HSM/KMS master keys for regulatory compliance
- Automatic key rotation without service interruption
- Tamper-evident audit trails for compliance
- Incident response procedures for cryptographic incidents

